    "title": "Taking Inventory - Signalis",
    "description": "Step into the world of Signalis with this interactive, reactive wallpaper inspired by the game’s inventory screen.\r\n\r\nWhat began as a visual showcase has evolved into a fully dynamic system. Items, status, UI, and effects now interact in real time, creating a constantly shifting state that responds to itself.\r\n\r\nA randomised item cycle, dynamic health system, and escalating status conditions drive visual instability across the interface. As the system degrades, UI elements flicker, diagnostics become erratic, and behaviour grows increasingly chaotic. Recovery is possible, but never guaranteed.\r\n\r\nMemory Fragments appear as brief interruptions, breaking the flow and reinforcing the fragmented, unstable atmosphere.\r\n\r\nAlongside these systems, the wallpaper features two functional visualisers, a media player, interchangeable character logos, a VHS-style clock, and layered post-processing effects.\r\n\r\nEvery element is designed to create a living, reactive interpretation of Signalis.",
